   "evidence": "Proof body: `have : Finite (orbit G S) := Subtype.finite; ... Finite.of_equiv (orbit G S) (orbitEquivQuotientStabilizer G S); exact Subgroup.finiteIndex_of_finite_quotient`. The only finset-specific step is the `Finite (Finset \u03b1)` instance. Grep shows no general version in Mathlib (`index_stabilizer` at Mathlib/GroupTheory/Index.lean:949 gives only the ncard formula).",
   "file": "TauCeti/GroupTheory/GroupAction/Stabilizer/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "State it as `theorem finiteIndex_stabilizer {G X : Type*} [Group G] [MulAction G X] [Finite X] (x : X) : (stabilizer G x).FiniteIndex` (orbit is finite \u2192 `orbitEquivQuotientStabilizer` \u2192 `finiteIndex_of_finite_quotient`). At the three uses (`VirtualCharacter.lean:344,353,373`) apply it with `X := Finset (G \u29f8 U)`, whose `Finite` instance comes from `Finite (G \u29f8 U)`.",
   "issue": "`MulAction.finiteIndex_stabilizer_finset` only covers finsets (`[Finite \u03b1] [DecidableEq \u03b1] (S : Finset \u03b1)`), but its proof only uses that the orbit lies in a finite type. Nothing about `S` being a finset is used, so the statement is narrower than its natural form.",
   "line": 649
  }
 ],
